                        "sense_id": "a18cbbb6-fcfe-3987-9194-a9dfc6fdba79",
                        "entry_id": "7123fb65-d1c5-36e7-9adb-24968ca5302e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A time (often an annual season) during which an area is flooded; the season when a river floods its banks."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e05b5cb9-8f50-437f-b054-bd9b7a5d9777",
                                "sense_id": "a18cbbb6-fcfe-3987-9194-a9dfc6fdba79",
                                "text": "Now, on the way, he came to a big, rushing river, which neither he nor his army could cross, for it was flood-time and the water was full of dangerous whirlpools, where nixies and water wraiths lived, always ready to drown men."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ab66bed-83b2-4787-9315-4b4d9b8d24c7",
                                "sense_id": "a18cbbb6-fcfe-3987-9194-a9dfc6fdba79",
                                "text": "In good seasons the stream must have been a fair little river, and during flood time it had spread all over the flat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "51cb5113-8dad-42be-a5b3-85f29b468559",
                                "sense_id": "a18cbbb6-fcfe-3987-9194-a9dfc6fdba79",
                                "text": "The storm that raged in him to-night could not uproot this hatred, the mightiest tree in all John’s country, all that remained to-night, in this, John’s floodtime."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79ada755-8300-4c74-8e3d-1339f04d9ea5",
                                "sense_id": "a18cbbb6-fcfe-3987-9194-a9dfc6fdba79",
                                "text": "Each year, the river brought its deposit of rich, red silt at floodtime. When the flood receded, the Mohave planted his corn, his squash and beans."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
